# Recorded outcome of `make -C tb frozen && make -C tb check-frozen', i.e. the 2001
# port of binutils 2.11.2 (tb/ref.7z) built on a current host, linking the 2001
# precompiled objects (tb/base2001.7z), against the reference ROMs base.7z ships.
#
# The 2001 toolchain does not reproduce those ROMs and is not expected to: it does
# not carry the stock 2.47 `lang_one_common' alignment, so every internal-RAM
# address after .bss sits 8 bytes lower. What must not change unnoticed is HOW FAR
# it is. `tb/romdiff.py --expect' reads this file and exits nonzero on any movement,
# which is what makes .github/workflows/frozen.yml able to go red.
#
# THREE columns are required per project, and romdiff.py refuses a line with fewer
# rather than defaulting the missing one. The third column, the size of the ROM the
# frozen toolchain produced, is here because this file was able to go stale without
# it: when `*(reset_network)' was restored in lib/www51.sc every ROM on both sides
# grew by three bytes, so the differing-byte counts did not move and a two-column
# file went on passing against inputs it no longer described.
#
# Re-derived, not copied: binutils 2.11.2 built here with `gcc -m32' (gcc 13.3.0,
# 2026-08-26), `make -C tb check-frozen' run against base.7z as it now stands, and
# `tb/romdiff.py' run over the result. The differing-byte counts came out byte for
# byte the ones recorded before, which is the expected outcome of a three-byte
# section restored identically on both sides; the ROM sizes are three bytes larger
# than the pre-restore run and are now recorded.
#
# diag does not link under 2.11.2: `lib/www51.sc:266: undefined symbol `_reti_'
# referenced in expression'. 2.11.2 folds a PROVIDE's right-hand side before it
# consults the destination, so the ten unused interrupt trampolines have to resolve
# even though diag references none of them. A linker difference, not an object one.
#
# project  outcome       differing bytes   ROM size
diag       not-produced  0                 0
ds1620     differ        217               6284
ds1822     differ        225               6078
lcd        differ        214               5754
led1       differ        213               5173
led2       differ        214               5010
led3       differ        214               5200
serial     differ        325               8128
welcome    differ        213               4812
wjava      differ        213               4812
